<title>UK: SOCCER-NORTHERN IRELAND DRAW 0-0 WITH PORTUGAL.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-NORTHERN IRELAND DRAW 0-0 WITH PORTUGAL.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Ireland drew 0-0 with Portugal in their group nine qualifier at Windsor Park on Saturday.</p>
<p>ATTENDANCE: 9,392.</p>
<p>TEAMS:</p>
<p>Northern Ireland: 1-Tommy Wright; 7-Keith Gillespie, 4-Colin Hill, 3-Stephen Morrow, 5-Gerry Taggart, 2-Ian Nolan; 6-Stephen Lomas, 10-Neil Lennon, 8-Jim Magilton; 9-Iain Dowie, 11-James Quinn (17-Gerard McMahon, 69).</p>
<p>Portugal: 1-Vitor Baia; 11-Paulinho Santos, 5-Fernando Couto, 2-Jorge Costa, 3-Dimas (18-Jorge Cadete 62); 9-Sergio Conceicao, 6-Paulo Sousa, 10-Rui Costa, 4-Oceano (15-Pedro Martins 62), 7-Figo; 8-Joao Pinto.</p>
<p>  Standings	   P   W   D   L   F   A  Pts    </p>
<p> Portugal	     6   2   3   1   5   2   9</p>
<p> Northern Ireland   5   1   3   1   4   3   6</p>
<p> Ukraine		3   2   0   1   3   2   6</p>
<p> Germany		3   1   2   0   6   2   5</p>
<p> Armenia		4   0   3   1   3   7   3</p>
<p> Albania		3   0   1   2   1   6   1</p>
